Data_Sources:
Police information system used by the Greater The Hague Police Force;
- Population registration data system (GBA);
- National database of demographic, social, and economic information on postal code areas in the Netherlands

Police information system of The Hague Police Service;
- Population registration data from BRP (nationwide information system);
- Community survey from the Study of Peers, Activities and Neighborhoods (SPAN) project;
- LISA data (Landelijk Informatiesysteem Arbeidsplaatsen);
- Census-like statistics from Statistics Netherlands

Independent_Variables:
1. Rivers;
2. Major roads with access control;
3. Major roads without access control;
4. Social barriers (Offender Hukou status and community majority Hukou status combinations);
5. Distance from home;
6. Proportion of houses built after 2000;
7. Average rent price;
8. Proportion of high-rise building;
9. Number of households (logged)

Data_Sources:
Existing dataset previously used for a social network analysis of PIRA's active core members;
- The Irish Times newspaper archives;
- Northern Ireland Statistics and Research Agency (NISRA);
- Conflict and Politics in Northern Ireland web service (CAIN);
- Ordnance Survey of Northern Ireland

Police data from the Metropolitan Police Service for riot-related incidents in London during August 2011;
- 2001 U.K. Census data for population churn rates and ethnic heterogeneity;
- Index of Multiple Deprivation (IMD) 2010 from the U.K. Department for Communities and Local Government;
- U.K. Department of Education data for school counts;
- Valuation Office Agency floor space data for 2004;
- Open Street Map data for underground station locations
